# Every way one deb822 stanza can be unusable. None of them may produce a
# Source, and every one of them must produce a problem: a wrong answer here is
# far worse than a missing one, and a silent skip is worse than either.

# 0: a line that is neither a field nor the continuation of one.
Types: deb
URIs: https://example.invalid/repo
this line has no colon at all
Suites: stable
Components: main

# 1: the same field twice, so which value applies is anyone's guess.
Types: deb
URIs: https://a.example/one
URIs: https://b.example/two
Suites: stable
Components: main

# 2: a Packages stanza that wandered into a sources file.
Package: hello
Version: 2.10-3
Description: not an apt source at all

# 3: a template that was never expanded.
Types: deb
URIs: https://example.invalid/${codename}
Suites: ${codename}
Components: main

# 4: a suite, but no component, and apt has no default for one.
Types: deb
URIs: https://example.invalid/repo
Suites: stable

# 5: source packages only.
Types: deb-src
URIs: https://example.invalid/repo
Suites: stable
Components: main

# 6: a type that does not exist.
Types: deb-foo
URIs: https://example.invalid/repo
Suites: stable
Components: main

# 7: a flat repository, which has no dists/ hierarchy to read.
Types: deb
URIs: https://vendor.example/flat
Suites: ./
